{title: Better Than a Slave}
{subtitle: Philemon 1:15–18; 1:10; 1:12–17; Colossians 4:7–9}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]He was separated [F/A]from you for a while
[Gm7]So that you might have him back for[Eb]ever [F/A]
[Bb]My child Onesi[F/A]mus born in my chains
[Gm7]A spiritual fa[Eb]ther in prison's [F]silence
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Bb]I am sending him [Dm7]back to you now
[Gm]And with him goes my very [Eb]heart [F/A]
[Bb]I would have liked [Dm7]to keep him near
To [Eb]serve me in your [F]place so [Bb]dear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F/A]No [Bb]longer as a slave [F]to be
But [Gm]better than a slave as [Eb]free
A dear [Bb]brother in the Lord is [F]he
Dear to [Gm]me but dearer to [Eb]you
[Bb]Welcome him [Dm7]as you would welcome [Eb]me
[Cm7]For we are [F]partners in this [Bb]new decree
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If he has wronged you [Dm7]in any way
[Gm]Or owes you anything that [Eb]is paid [F]
[Bb]Charge it to me [Dm7]I am the debt
In the [Eb]gospel truth [F]we do not [Bb]fret
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Tychicus [F]speaks of [Bb]my situation
[Eb]Beloved [F]brother and [Bb]faithful servant
[Eb]Onesimus [F]comes [Dm7]with them to [Gm]tell
The [Cm7]faithful brother we [F7sus4]can [F]well
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
No [Bb]longer as a slave [F]to be
But [Gm]better than a slave as [Eb]free
A dear [Bb]brother in the Lord is [F]he
Dear to [Gm]me but dearer to [Eb]you
[Bb]Welcome him [Dm7]as you would welcome [Eb]me
[Cm7]For we are [F]partners in this [Bb]new decree
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Your kindness voluntary and [Bb]free [Bb/D][Gm7]
[Eb]Welcome him as you would welcome [Bb][Bb/D]me [Gm7][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
